<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tikar people</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tikar are a people of the Tikar plain in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cameroon">Cameroon</a>. Many of the ruling dynasties of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cameroon-grassfields">Cameroon Grassfields</a>, including those of Bamum, Nso and Bafut, trace their origins to Tikar princes or princesses who left their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> and founded new kingdoms, so that Tikar origin became a mark of royal descent. Their language belongs to the Bantoid branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a>–Congo family.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tikar-people.jpg" alt="Tikar people" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Happiraphael · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FluteNordOuest.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
